  "geometry72_cached_probe_matches_excluded_v10_initial_hashes": true,
  "finding": "Fresh-generation and subsequent cache-loaded runs differ only in terrain-derived policy terms (base height and foothold hints). Two independently repeated cache-loaded pairs are bit-identical for every captured tensor. This supports generation-vs-OBJ-cache roundtrip as the cause; no observation rounding or zeroing applied.",
  "mechanism": "Isaac Lab returns in-memory mesh on cache miss and loads mesh.obj on hit; trimesh OBJ export defaults to 8 decimal digits.",
  "limits": "The cache is a shared local directory. Manifest equality is enforced before and after every process; it does not alone prove imported scene identity. Exact full initial state AND 88D observation hashes remain mandatory. Geometry74 is diagnostic only."
